{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$g : Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$g \\circ f$", "MATH_0004": "$g$", "MATH_0005": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quasi-compact-permanence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3eedd68d58144ad734232a5a86bea9f93f32d89d0c65b55a4e67108c06ae72f4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b02e47bc382b57004af86e53bbcb9bad777377245923f3279911f99af134d211", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be morphisms of schemes.\nIf <MATH_0003> is quasi-compact and <MATH_0004> is quasi-separated\nthen <MATH_0005> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ce8cb3b5711efc6fb0f08797634bba25a25e6f3c6828b67e9076a833c1f0b20c", "unit_id": "tag:03GI:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$(1, f) : X \\to X \\times_Z Y \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\times_Z Y \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$g$", "MATH_0005": "$g \\circ f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-section-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-separated-permanence}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-compact-preserved-base-change}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-composition-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ef43922252320be233b8f4db25dc955db7ce207c558236205e1049a76b540eca", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a1701f9cda38fd57571be5dec04d29c42896951230ad3d0b6efcaac1f84f82e", "source_text": "This is true because <MATH_0001> equals the composition\n<MATH_0002>. The first map\nis quasi-compact by Lemma <REF_0001>\nbecause it is a section of the quasi-separated morphism <MATH_0003>\n(a base change of <MATH_0004>, see Lemma <REF_0002>).\nThe second map is quasi-compact as it\nis the base change of <MATH_0005>, see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nAnd compositions of quasi-compact\nmorphisms are quasi-compact, see Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:20c99d7fb8a56fbee686cf37573741dfa86769743ec89e66a3168a5b5cce6512", "unit_id": "tag:03GI:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-affine-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c3978146dc78a4ffed39869af1f823a6bc55d837f6f4b73af2ef17d2fbaaa35d", "source_text": "An affine scheme is separated. A morphism from an affine scheme\nto another scheme is separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eb83a01c0640dda7503e6109d16dfe77c97425685bc499db109598efb62f934c", "unit_id": "tag:01KN:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U = \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to X \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-affines-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-separated}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-compose-after-separated}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fe5be81a093be5dee81a143e587d90e820ee50f1c174ade223a0fcaaa2b82043", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2451ce330e3c6a843b65dc02f0f8e95340ceb3c7bab1762a3556ed400fbb312e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. Then <MATH_0002>\nhas closed diagonal by Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThus <MATH_0003> is separated by Definition <REF_0002>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is a morphism of schemes, then we can apply\nLemma <REF_0003>\nto the morphisms <MATH_0005> to conclude\nthat <MATH_0006> is separated.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:74bf974f2ee0bed1595fb333b39d7a47f8c935d8acdfa0aa5bea1def0d9657ef", "unit_id": "tag:01KN:proof"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:79cc972e1883926566e998fe9e9a74573586fced33101fbd36c7c31db320e500", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nYou may have been wondering whether the condition\nof only considering pairs of affine opens whose image is contained\nin an affine open is really necessary to be able to conclude\nthat their intersection is affine. Often it isn't!\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7dc75930da25beccdd9d4a56829e877923ea7e993c3d62164b14a960158e2220", "unit_id": "tag:01KH:prose-0003"}
